{
  "date": "2026-07-31",
  "period_start": "2026-07-01",
  "period_end": "2026-07-31",
  "title": "More things than pixels",
  "summary": "July turned Pollinations into a broader creative workbench: 3D, vectors, music, richer audio, agent tools, and a rapidly expanding model garden all arrived through the same familiar APIs.\n\n3D generation arrived with Trellis 2 and Rodin 2.5, followed by Recraft SVG output, Lyria music clips, richer ElevenLabs dialogue and isolation tools, OCR, transcription, and longer-running Wan video jobs. The API spent the month acquiring formats.\n\nNew GPT, Claude, Gemini, Grok, Qwen, Mistral, Cohere, NVIDIA, image, audio, and video models expanded the unified endpoint, while embeddings gained multimodal and role-aware search support. Better descriptions, search, access labels, and mobile cards made the growing catalog less archaeological.\n\nModel builders gained private testing before publication, readable model titles, image-generation and edit support, configurable fallbacks, and delegated agent tokens. The Greenhouse also added a substantial crop of community apps, from creative studios to chat tools, storybooks, games, and Roblox infrastructure.\n\nPollen activity gained accurate, scrollable history and daily charts; Enter moved to shareable routes; model discovery became faster and clearer; and public media galleries gave tagged creations durable, attributable homes.",
  "pr_count": 288,
